   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "M2.4: the MIDI type (M5_MIDI).\n\nInput: m5_duo_cc.mid (copied into input/ by the workflow runner; otherwise copy it from custom_nodes/com5fy/workflows/inputs/). Clarinet + piano, 100 BPM in 3/4, 75 BPM from bar 3, 4/4 from bar 4. The clarinet's 4th note (A4) is bent up a quarter tone; a modulation (CC1) swell runs over bars 1-2; the piano holds the sustain pedal in bar 2.\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. Loaded MIDI (Preview as Text): 2 tracks with their channels, note counts and controller lanes (CC1 modulation, pitch bend, CC64 sustain). The real MIDI viewer (piano roll) is M3.4.\n2. MIDI as a Sequence: two staves, Clarinet (the A4 with a +50 cents quarter-tone sharp) and Piano (4 three-note chords).\n3. ... as a Score: 3/4 with a 100 BPM mark, 75 BPM at bar 3, 4/4 at bar 4, read from the MIDI file's tempo map.\n4. CC1 as a BPF, read-only (green): a step curve 0 -> 100 -> 20, range 0-127. Set lane to \"pitch bend\" for the bend in cents, or cc 64 for the pedal.\n5. Bottom row, the other way: the M2.1 duo score -> Sequence -> MIDI -> Save MIDI. Velocities come from the dynamics (p = 49, mf = 80, f = 96...); the flute's quarter-flat becomes a pitch bend (see Saved MIDI's 'pitch bend (2)': bend and reset). The file lands in output/m5/ (path in the Save MIDI output); open it in a DAW or notation program.\n\nTry: your own .mid files (put them in input/ and press R); a channel or track number in MIDI to BPF when several tracks have the same controller. An absent lane gives an error listing the lanes the file has."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
